erified":true},{"surface":"அரசு","parts":[{"text":"அரசு","lemma":"aracu","gloss":"kingship/government"}],"gloss":"kingship"},{"surface":"கெழு","parts":[{"text":"கெழு","lemma":"keḻu","gloss":"having/associated with"}],"gloss":"having"},{"surface":"திருவே","parts":[{"text":"திரு","lemma":"tiru","gloss":"wealth/fortune"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"emphasis/vocative"}],"gloss":"wealth indeed"}]}],"literal":"Elders [after] elders, [as] death carried [them] away, / destiny to give, the came ancient victorious inheritance / \"We attained [it], if so, we attained greatness,\" saying, / begging [for] taxes [from] citizens, without sharp manliness, / if a small man obtains [it], that is not great indeed! / Thronging battle bearing, strength-possessing, enduring-effort / if a great man obtains [it], [like] in low water / dry pond's side, a small stick of white corkwood / in the hot sun withering and drying up, very / light indeed is it, without blemish, / touching the sky, the raised white umbrella / of kings with drums, the kingship-possessing wealth!","translation":"When death carries away elders after elders, the ancient, victorious inheritance of the kingdom comes to one as destined. If a small, weak-minded man who begs for taxes from his citizens obtains it, thinking, 'We have attained it, and thus we have attained greatness,' it is not a great thing indeed. But if a great, strong, and enduring warrior who bears the brunt of intense battles obtains it, then the royal wealth of kings who possess drums and white umbrellas raised to touch the sky is as light and trivial as a small piece of white corkwood withering and drying up under the hot sun at the edge of a dry pond.","modern":"மூதாதையர்கள் ஒவ்வொருவராக எமன் கொண்டு செல்ல, விதிப்படியே நமக்குக் கிடைத்த பழமையான, வெற்றி பொருந்திய அரசுரிமையை, 'நாம் அடைந்துவிட்டோம், அதனால் பெருமை அடைந்துவிட்டோம்' என்று எண்ணி, தன் குடிமக்களிடம் வரி கேட்டு இரக்கும் கூர்மையற்ற ஆண்மையுடைய சிறியோன் பெற்றால், அது சிறந்தது அன்று. ஆனால், நெருங்கி வரும் போரைத் தாங்கும் வலிமையும் விடாமுயற்சியும் உடைய பெரியோன் பெற்றால், குற்றம் அற்ற, வானை முட்டும் வெண்கொற்றக் குடையும் முரசும் கொண்ட வேந்தர்களின் அரசுரிமையாகிய செல்வமானது, நீர் வற்றிய குளத்தின் கரையில் கிடக்கும் சிறிய வெள்ளைக் கிடை மரத்துண்டு வெயிலில் காய்ந்து உலர்ந்து போவது போல, மிகவும் எளிதானதாகத் தோன்றும்.","explanation":"This poem is spoken by the Chola king Nalankilli under the theme of Porunmolik Kanci (counseling on impermanence and virtue). The king reflects on the nature of royal power and wealth, comparing how different rulers perceive it. A weak, petty ruler (siriyon) views the inherited kingdom as a grand achievement and exploits his citizens for taxes. In contrast, a truly great and heroic ruler (vilumiyon) views the vast royal wealth and power as something extremely light and trivial, like a dry piece of corkwood (venkitai) withering under the hot sun. The poem uses the vivid image of a dry pond and withered corkwood to illustrate the insignificance of material wealth to a noble mind. Key words include 'siriyon' (small man), 'vilumiyon' (great man), and 'noytu' (light/trivial).","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.7],[0.7,1.26],[1.26,1.6],[1.81,2.1],[2.1,3.0],[3.0,3.3],[3.3,3.7],[3.7,3.9],[3.9,5.3],[5.3,5.5],[5.5,5.7],[5.7,6.2],[6.2,6.6],[6.6,7.8],[7.8,8.4],[8.4,8.6],[8.6,8.9],[8.9,10.2],[10.2,10.7],[10.7,11.2],[11.2,11.68],[11.68,12.8],[12.8,13.2],[13.2,13.55],[13.55,13.9],[13.9,15.1],[15.1,15.5],[15.5,15.9],[15.9,16.1],[16.1,16.9],[17.1,17.6],[17.6,17.8],[17.8,18.5],[19.38,19.74],[19.74,20.54],[20.54,20.84],[20.84,21.24],[21.24,22.14],[22.14,22.54],[22.54,22.74],[22.74,23.34],[23.34,24.06],[24.06,24.54],[24.54,25.24],[25.24,25.77],[25.94,26.34],[26.34,26.77],[26.94,27.34]],"female":[[0.0,0.7],[0.7,1.26],[1.26,1.6],[1.77,2.0],[2.0,2.71],[3.0,3.3],[3.3,3.7],[3.7,3.9],[3.9,5.8],[5.8,6.0],[6.0,6.2],[6.2,6.7],[6.7,7.2],[7.2,8.2],[8.2,9.0],[9.0,9.2],[9.2,9.5],[9.5,11.1],[11.1,11.7],[11.7,12.3],[12.3,12.81],[12.81,14.0],[14.0,14.4],[14.